                "username": "jagpalgill"
            },
            "kind": "REWORK",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Software/Update.events.yaml",
                    "line": 57,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "Why are we adding this when it isn't in the Redfish spec?  There is a zero-Arg UpdateInProgress there that doesn't seem very useful.  What is the anticipated frequency this will be emitted?  Why do we need this event separate from TargetDetermined (which means the update is starting) and the conclusion events?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Software/Update.events.yaml",
                    "line": 57,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jagpal S Gill",
                        "email": "paligill@gmail.com",
                        "username": "jagpalgill"
                    },
                    "message": "> Why are we adding this when it isn't in the Redfish spec?  There is a zero-Arg UpdateInProgress there that doesn't seem very useful.  What is the anticipated frequency this will be emitted?  Why do we need this event separate from TargetDetermined (which means the update is starting) and the conclusion events?\n\n\nI had discussed with Redfish maintainers on DMTF and they don't want to provide a new message with the targetName, hence i had added this message to openBMC Namespace. Their reasoning was around the fact that percentage progress is already covered in task and there are other messages which provides lower level details per targetName, hence this new message will seem redundant. \n\nFrom usability perspective it could probably be useful for long running upgrades but we always have task progress percentage for same purpose too. Hence, for now i am going to skip this message from the list and will revisit it later when there are more concrete usecases/needs."
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Software/Update.events.yaml",
                    "line": 90,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "Why is this one not ResetRequired?  \"ResetDevice\" is ambiguous if the device did reset or the device needs a reset."
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Software/Update.events.yaml",
                    "line": 90,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jagpal S Gill",
                        "email": "paligill@gmail.com",
                        "username": "jagpalgill"
                    },
                    "message": "Done, changed to ResetRequired."
                }
            ],
